From e5cfc23bd6d21b376cc2ed76d584d94e95a7aed4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?S=C3=A9bastien=20Taylor?= <sebastien@au-zone.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 16:51:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] OS08a20: pass pclk, not &pclk, to VVSENSORIOC_S_CLK
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

pclk is already a pointer, so the ioctl received the address of the local
pointer variable. Compare VVSENSORIOC_G_CLK, which passes pclk.

Latent rather than active: the vvcam os08a20 handler for S_CLK is a no-op
that never dereferences arg, so nothing observable changes on this sensor.
Corrected so it stays correct if that handler is ever implemented.

Signed-off-by: Sébastien Taylor <sebastien@au-zone.com>
---
 units/isi/drv/OS08a20/source/OS08a20.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/units/isi/drv/OS08a20/source/OS08a20.c b/units/isi/drv/OS08a20/source/OS08a20.c
index 958bcf6..ff72fbf 100644
--- a/units/isi/drv/OS08a20/source/OS08a20.c
+++ b/units/isi/drv/OS08a20/source/OS08a20.c
@@ -135,7 +135,7 @@ static RESULT OS08A20_IsiSensorSetClkIss(IsiSensorHandle_t handle,
     if (pclk == NULL)
         return RET_NULL_POINTER;
     
-    ret = ioctl(pHalCtx->sensor_fd, VVSENSORIOC_S_CLK, &pclk);
+    ret = ioctl(pHalCtx->sensor_fd, VVSENSORIOC_S_CLK, pclk);
     if (ret != 0) {
         TRACE(OS08A20_ERROR, "%s set clk error: %s\n", __func__,
               strerror(errno));
-- 
